// Must not compile: "duplicate declaration; names are case-insensitive, so STORE.SET is
// the same name as store.set".
//
// Names are case-insensitive and the dot is cosmetic, so STORE.SET and store.set are ONE
// name. The message used to stop at "duplicate declaration", which reads as though the
// name itself were taken -- so the writer picks a different name instead of understanding
// why. The result is visible in the sources: STORE.OPSET and CURVE.NDAYS exist only to
// dodge a collision nobody explained. Ten of the fifteen namespace errors in the error
// log are this case.
//
// tests/compiler/name_case_collision_same.wz is the other half: a collision WITHOUT
// capitals must not get the extra sentence, or the explanation becomes noise.
import store;
const
  STORE.SET = 1;
begin
end.
